# Paths that need Kelly's review before they reach main.
#
# Not every file: collaborators can review and merge ordinary app changes among themselves.
# These are the files that decide what CI runs, what a release build compiles and signs,
# what the website publishes, and where secrets go. Release and deploy runs execute main's
# copy of them with the secrets of the azure-signing, relay and live-smoke environments in
# reach (and the github-pages deploy permission), so a change here that slipped through
# review could reach those secrets, the signing certificate or the live site at the next
# release or deploy. With code-owner review required on main, a change to any of them waits
# for @kellylford.
#
# Every rule names the same owner, so their order does not matter.

# CI: workflows, the pinned vpk version, Dependabot, and this file itself.
/.github/                          @kellylford

# The bug-report relay: main pushes under relay/ deploy to Cloudflare automatically.
/relay/                            @kellylford

# Test projects and the fixtures library they build. Tests run inside the release build job,
# before signing, in the same job that holds the release credentials.
/QuickMail.Tests/                  @kellylford
/QuickMail.IntegrationTests/       @kellylford
/Tools/                            @kellylford

# Build and packaging: MSBuild inputs (anything here runs during the release build), the SDK
# pin, the solution, the local build script, and the installer and winget configuration.
/Directory.Build.props             @kellylford
/global.json                       @kellylford
/QuickMail.sln                     @kellylford
/build.bat                         @kellylford
*.csproj                           @kellylford
*.props                            @kellylford
*.targets                          @kellylford
nuget.config                       @kellylford
NuGet.config                       @kellylford
/installer/                        @kellylford

# Scripts CI runs: credential partials, test servers, the release-history generator the
# Pages deploy uses, the winget matrix probe.
/scripts/                          @kellylford

# What the release and the Pages site publish verbatim.
/docs/USER-GUIDE.md                @kellylford
/docs/release-notes-*.md           @kellylford
/docs/download-footer.md           @kellylford
/docs/reporting-issues-footer.md   @kellylford
/docs/privacy.html                 @kellylford
/docs/github-release-download-numbers.md  @kellylford
/docs/*.Credentials.example        @kellylford
